     paragraph, boxed text and paragraphs before the first section. -->
<book-part-wrapper xmlns="http://example.org/synthetic-bits" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink">
  <book-part book-part-type="chapter" id="article-90002">
    <book-part-meta>
      <title-group><title>Acute Kidney Injury</title></title-group>
      <contrib-group>
        <contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Achebe</surname><given-names>Ngozi</given-names></name></contrib>
        <contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Berg</surname><given-names>Lars-Erik</given-names></name></contrib>
        <contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Costa</surname><given-names>Rui</given-names></name></contrib>
        <contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Dubois</surname><given-names>Claire</given-names></name></contrib>
      </contrib-group>
      <pub-date><year>2024</year></pub-date>
    </book-part-meta>
    <body>
      <p>Acute kidney injury is a sudden fall in kidney function over hours to days.</p>
      <sec><title>Evaluation</title>
        <p>Staging uses serum creatinine and urine output:<list list-type="order"><list-item><p>Stage 1: creatinine 1.5 to 1.9 times baseline.</p></list-item><list-item><p>Stage 3: creatinine three times baseline, or renal replacement therapy.</p></list-item></list></p>
        <boxed-text><title>Key point</title><p>Oliguria lasting more than 12 hours suggests a severe injury.</p></boxed-text>
      </sec>
      <sec><title>Prognosis</title>
        <p>Patients with acute kidney injury in intensive care stay longer and have a higher mortality.</p>
      </sec>
      <sec><title>References</title><p>Should be skipped.</p></sec>
    </body>
  </book-part>
</book-part-wrapper>
